{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00272",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.89,
      "end_seconds": 4.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "Sorry, doctor, I couldn't find the door at first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.47,
      "end_seconds": 8.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Yes, do sit. Tell me what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 8.98,
      "end_seconds": 12.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "It's a burning pain in the upper tummy, mostly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 15.84,
      "end_seconds": 17.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "And when did that start?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 18.83,
      "end_seconds": 26.64,
      "duration_seconds": 7.81,
      "text": "Probably about a month. Yeah. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.0,
      "end_seconds": 34.92,
      "duration_seconds": 7.92,
      "text": "Go on. Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.1,
      "end_seconds": 40.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "I'd say severe. It's once or twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.32,
      "end_seconds": 42.62,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "Have you had nausea?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.62,
      "end_seconds": 49.98,
      "duration_seconds": 6.36,
      "text": "Well, yeah. Ten days, I'd say. Okay, so as for nausea, it's severe, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.78,
      "end_seconds": 54.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "Have you been able to keep up with your usual activities?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.44,
      "end_seconds": 69.99,
      "duration_seconds": 13.55,
      "text": "For the most part, uh, yes. I just carry on and try not to dwell on things too much, though I won't pretend it hasn't crossed my mind a few times."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.34,
      "end_seconds": 72.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "Any fever or black stools?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.69,
      "end_seconds": 76.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "So, no. None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.01,
      "end_seconds": 79.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Right. Any trouble swallowing or vomiting blood?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 80.8,
      "end_seconds": 85.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "I haven't had trouble swallowing or vomiting blood, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.81,
      "end_seconds": 89.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "I'll try to keep this as efficient as I can."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.6,
      "end_seconds": 92.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "Thank you, I appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.25,
      "end_seconds": 97.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.28,
      "end_seconds": 110.7,
      "duration_seconds": 9.42,
      "text": "Well, I've had arthritis in my knees for five years now. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.47,
      "end_seconds": 112.17,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Mm-hm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.44,
      "end_seconds": 122.53,
      "duration_seconds": 9.09,
      "text": "Yes, acid reflux. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't. It's the not knowing that gets to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.85,
      "end_seconds": 128.92,
      "duration_seconds": 6.07,
      "text": "Okay, acid reflux, that's already on your record. Good to know. Did you manage to eat before coming?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.65,
      "end_seconds": 133.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "So, yes, I had something small this morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.15,
      "end_seconds": 141.25,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "Are you on any tablets or medication? I'll explain everything as we go along."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.45,
      "end_seconds": 147.8,
      "duration_seconds": 5.35,
      "text": "Pantoprazole. I take it 40 milligrams, before breakfast for my acidity."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.39,
      "end_seconds": 164.34,
      "duration_seconds": 15.95,
      "text": "What I'm doing here is putting together three things: what you tell me, what I find when I examine you, and what the tests show. None of those alone is enough, which is why we sometimes need to wait for results before being certain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.06,
      "end_seconds": 167.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "I appreciate you explaining that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.44,
      "end_seconds": 170.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Have you had any surgery before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.23,
      "end_seconds": 176.41,
      "duration_seconds": 5.18,
      "text": "Right, I had my tonsils out when I was a child."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.32,
      "end_seconds": 180.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "I want to open your previous notes quickly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.92,
      "end_seconds": 181.9,
      "duration_seconds": 0.98,
      "text": "Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.6,
      "end_seconds": 197.02,
      "duration_seconds": 5.42,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.2,
      "end_seconds": 200.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "No, nothing I'm aware of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.02,
      "end_seconds": 212.41,
      "duration_seconds": 11.39,
      "text": "I like to make sure you understand what's happening, so please stop me at any point. There are no silly questions, and I'd much rather you ask now than go home still wondering about something."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.71,
      "end_seconds": 215.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "Right, I understand now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.13,
      "end_seconds": 219.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "I'll just check what's already recorded here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 220.54,
      "end_seconds": 221.51,
      "duration_seconds": 0.97,
      "text": "Please do."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.85,
      "end_seconds": 234.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Is it okay if I type while we talk?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.13,
      "end_seconds": 237.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Yes, of course, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.45,
      "end_seconds": 255.73,
      "duration_seconds": 17.28,
      "text": "So, based on your history, this looks most like gastritis. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had a burning pain in the upper tummy for about a month, severe, and no vomiting blood or trouble swallowing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 257.17,
      "end_seconds": 259.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "Oh, exactly, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.67,
      "end_seconds": 267.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "Do you have everything you need to get home alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 268.67,
      "end_seconds": 281.24,
      "duration_seconds": 12.57,
      "text": "Yes, I've got my transport sorted. It's a bit of a trek, but I'm used to the journey by now, and I brought something to read for the wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.59,
      "end_seconds": 285.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "We should do an H. pylori test for dyspepsia."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 287.02,
      "end_seconds": 290.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "Uh, alright. When can I do that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.25,
      "end_seconds": 293.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Let's get blood tests, for dyspepsia."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 294.33,
      "end_seconds": 295.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "Okay, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.31,
      "end_seconds": 321.55,
      "duration_seconds": 25.24,
      "text": "Avoid spicy, oily food and don't take anti-inflammatory painkillers on an empty stomach. Try to keep a simple diary of when it happens and what you were doing, and bring it to the next visit. If you vomit blood or pass black stools, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department. Let's review you after the results are back. Can you run through the plan with me quickly, just to be certain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 322.9,
      "end_seconds": 328.76,
      "duration_seconds": 5.86,
      "text": "So, I come back after the results are back. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 329.71,
      "end_seconds": 334.91,
      "duration_seconds": 5.2,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. I think we've covered it. Do you have any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 335.96,
      "end_seconds": 339.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "That's all, thank you for your time."
    }
  ]
}